Plan for workload pg-main: Planned, site a to site b
Ledger: SiteFailover tack-system/pg-main-20261027-101500 at site b

Sites:
  a  Primary  declares a  healthy  Cluster db/pg-a: phase "Cluster in healthy state", declares pg-a primary, pod pg-a-1, timeline 1
  b  Replica  declares a  healthy  Cluster db/pg-b: phase "Cluster in healthy state", declares pg-a primary, pod pg-b-1, timeline 1
  c  Replica  declares a  healthy  Cluster db/pg-c: phase "Cluster in healthy state", declares pg-a primary, pod pg-c-1, timeline 1

Hold
   1. hold-a-cluster-pg-a  site a
      hold Cluster db/pg-a at site a: Flux stops applying it
        annotate Cluster db/pg-a: kustomize.toolkit.fluxcd.io/reconcile=disabled, failover.tako.id/held-by=pg-main-20261027-101500
        applied by Flux Kustomization flux-system/a
   2. reconcile-hold-a  site a
      reconcile Flux at site a, so no apply started before the hold is still in flight
        request a reconcile of Kustomizations flux-system/a and their GitRepository; wait up to 5m0s
   3. hold-b-cluster-pg-b  site b
      hold Cluster db/pg-b at site b: Flux stops applying it
        annotate Cluster db/pg-b: kustomize.toolkit.fluxcd.io/reconcile=disabled, failover.tako.id/held-by=pg-main-20261027-101500
        applied by Flux Kustomization flux-system/b
   4. reconcile-hold-b  site b
      reconcile Flux at site b, so no apply started before the hold is still in flight
        request a reconcile of Kustomizations flux-system/b and their GitRepository; wait up to 5m0s
   5. hold-c-cluster-pg-c  site c (waits for the site if unreachable)
      hold Cluster db/pg-c at site c: Flux stops applying it
        annotate Cluster db/pg-c: kustomize.toolkit.fluxcd.io/reconcile=disabled, failover.tako.id/held-by=pg-main-20261027-101500
        applied by Flux Kustomization flux-system/c
   6. reconcile-hold-c  site c (waits for the site if unreachable)
      reconcile Flux at site c, so no apply started before the hold is still in flight
        request a reconcile of Kustomizations flux-system/c and their GitRepository; wait up to 5m0s
Failover
   7. demote-a  site a
      demote Cluster pg-a: declare pg-b primary and drop any old token
        patch Cluster db/pg-a (merge): {"spec":{"replica":{"primary":"pg-b","promotionToken":null}}}
   8. wait-demoted-a  site a
      wait until Cluster pg-a has demoted and published its demotion token
        wait up to 10m0s on Cluster db/pg-a until:
          {.status.demotionToken} is not empty
          {.status.switchReplicaClusterStatus.inProgress} NotEquals "true"
   9. capture-token  site a
      record the demotion token of Cluster pg-a in the ledger
        record {.status.demotionToken} of Cluster db/pg-a in the ledger as $(demotionToken)
  10. promote-b  site b
      promote Cluster pg-b with the demotion token, in one patch
        patch Cluster db/pg-b (merge): {"spec":{"replica":{"primary":"pg-b","promotionToken":"$(demotionToken)"}}}
  11. wait-promoted-b  site b
      wait until Cluster pg-b has used the token and runs a healthy primary
        wait up to 10m0s on Cluster db/pg-b until:
          {.status.lastPromotionToken} Equals "$(demotionToken)"
          {.status.instancesReportedState.*.isPrimary} Contains "true"
          {.status.phase} Equals "Cluster in healthy state"
  12. clear-token-b  site b
      remove the used token from Cluster pg-b, so it can never apply again
        patch Cluster db/pg-b (merge): {"spec":{"replica":{"promotionToken":null}}}
  13. declare-c  site c (waits for the site if unreachable)
      make Cluster pg-c declare pg-b primary
        patch Cluster db/pg-c (merge): {"spec":{"replica":{"primary":"pg-b","promotionToken":null}}}
  14. verify-b  site b
      verify that Cluster pg-b is a healthy primary and declares itself
        wait up to 10m0s on Cluster db/pg-b until:
          {.spec.replica.primary} Equals "pg-b"
          {.status.instancesReportedState.*.isPrimary} Contains "true"
          {.status.phase} Equals "Cluster in healthy state"
PromoteToGitOps
  15. git-commit  Git
      commit the live state to https://git.example.com/gitops.git branch main
        clusters/a/cluster.yaml: spec.replica.primary = "pg-b"  (site a, Cluster db/pg-a spec.replica.primary)
        clusters/a/cluster.yaml: spec.replica.promotionToken removed  (site a, Cluster db/pg-a spec.replica.promotionToken)
        clusters/b/cluster.yaml: spec.replica.primary = "pg-b"  (site b, Cluster db/pg-b spec.replica.primary)
        clusters/b/cluster.yaml: spec.replica.promotionToken removed  (site b, Cluster db/pg-b spec.replica.promotionToken)
        clusters/c/cluster.yaml: spec.replica.primary = "pg-b"  (site c, Cluster db/pg-c spec.replica.primary)
        clusters/c/cluster.yaml: spec.replica.promotionToken removed  (site c, Cluster db/pg-c spec.replica.promotionToken)
        commit message: tack: pg-main primary a to b (planned)
  16. reconcile-git-a  site a
      wait for Flux at site a to apply the run's commit (held objects stay as they are)
        request a reconcile of Kustomizations flux-system/a and their GitRepository; wait up to 5m0s
        until Flux has applied $(git.commit)
  17. reconcile-git-b  site b
      wait for Flux at site b to apply the run's commit (held objects stay as they are)
        request a reconcile of Kustomizations flux-system/b and their GitRepository; wait up to 5m0s
